Vendored airunner_common (issue #2243, Gap 1)
============================================

What
----
`airunner_common/` is a byte-verified copy of the 13 pure-Python modules from
the airunner-common 6.1.8 wheel (no dist-info), shipped as files into
usr/lib/python3/dist-packages by debian/airunner.install.
`airunner-common.LICENSE` is the wheel's GPL-3.0-only license text.

Origin
------
- Distribution: airunner-common 6.1.8
- Source repository: https://github.com/Capsize-Games/airunner-common
- Source commit: 733b0f4c8fb38952866e9cf7be2cc69793a46e92
- Wheel: airunner_common-6.1.8-py3-none-any.whl
- Wheel SHA256: ac2110ecbcd965c9a773405494bcecb3d1c6c5f127d22fde81d37478b94088fd
- File and license hashes: debian/vendor/airunner-common.json

The wheel was built from the source commit above; it was not retrieved from
PyPI. Its RECORD hashes and sizes were verified. The 13 package modules match
the source commit byte-for-byte, and the license matches both the wheel and
source LICENSE.

Why vendored
------------
airunner-common~=6.1.8 is a hard services import (235 import sites), but
dh_python3 cannot map it to a distro package, so the .deb neither shipped it
nor depended on it and the installed daemon died with
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'airunner_common'. This mirrors the
airunner_native stanza in debian/airunner.install: pybuild cannot build two
source trees into one binary package, so the module ships as files. Nothing
queries airunner-common dist metadata at runtime (get_version() resolves
airunner-services first and falls back to package_metadata.VERSION), so no
dist-info is shipped.

The common runtime package requires python-dotenv at module import time;
debian/control declares python3-dotenv. Its legacy Shield requirement is an
optional extra, not a base dependency or an enabled runtime in this package.

Exit criteria
-------------
Delete this directory and ship a real dependency once either holds:

- Capsize-Games/airunner-common publishes its own Debian binary (the fix
  #2243 prefers), or
- dh_python3 can map airunner-common to a distro package.

Then replace the .install stanza below with that binary in debian/control
Depends.
